>The difference between markets and ecosystems is that markets are socially
>constructed mechanisms for exchanging goods and services, which operate on
>human timescales, products living and dying in a matter of years or
>decades--while ecosystems evolve over geologic timescales, contain
>millions of years of hard won genetic information, and are rapidly being
